WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.452
This six-stage workflow organizes the module.

00:00:02.452 --> 00:00:04.797
Profile first. Preserve the source.

00:00:04.797 --> 00:00:07.582
Normalize representation where the rule is known.

00:00:07.582 --> 00:00:10.272
Validate values against documented rules.

00:00:10.272 --> 00:00:13.897
Resolve duplicates or questionable rows with explicit logic.

00:00:13.897 --> 00:00:18.402
Finally, move stable rules closer to data entry through constraints or monitoring.

00:00:18.402 --> 00:00:23.132
The order matters because prevention should come after you understand the data and the rules.

00:00:23.132 --> 00:00:27.477
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:27.477 --> 00:00:32.962
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:32.962 --> 00:00:35.132
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:35.132 --> 00:00:41.052
In a real setting such as a healthcare pipeline validating contact, demographic, and event fields,

00:00:41.052 --> 00:00:46.582
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:46.582 --> 00:00:47.942
before discussing syntax.

00:00:47.942 --> 00:00:53.660
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
